🐍 String Methods in Python
A string is a sequence of characters written inside quotes.
name = "Preethi"
Python provides many built-in string methods to perform operations on strings.
1. upper()
Converts all letters to uppercase.
name = "preethi"
print(name.upper())
Output: PREETHI
2. lower()
Converts all letters to lowercase.
name = "PREETHI"
print(name.lower())
Output: preethi
3. capitalize()
Converts the first character to uppercase.
name = "python"
print(name.capitalize())
Output: Python
4. title()
Converts the first letter of every word to uppercase.
text = "python programming language"
print(text.title())
Output: Python Programming Language
5. strip()
Removes spaces from the beginning and end.
text = "  Python  "
print(text.strip())
Output: Python
6. replace()
Replaces one part of a string with another.
text = "I like Java"
print(text.replace("Java", "Python"))
Output: I like Python
7. find()
Returns the position (index) of a substring.
text = "Python"
print(text.find("t"))
Output: 2
8. count()
Counts how many times a character or substring occurs.
text = "banana"
print(text.count("a"))
Output: 3
9. startswith()
Checks whether a string starts with a particular value.
text = "Python"
print(text.startswith("Py"))
Output: True
10. endswith()
Checks whether a string ends with a particular value.
text = "Python"
print(text.endswith("on"))
Output: True
11. split()
Splits a string into a list.
text = "I love Python"
print(text.split())
Output:
['I', 'love', 'Python']
12. join()
Joins elements together using a specified separator.
words = ["I", "love", "Python"]
print(" ".join(words))
Output:
I love Python
13. isalpha()
Checks whether all characters are alphabets.
text = "Python"
print(text.isalpha())
Output: True
14. isdigit()
Checks whether all characters are digits.
num = "12345"
print(num.isdigit())
Output: True
15. isalnum()
Checks whether all characters are alphabets or numbers.
text = "Python123"
print(text.isalnum())
Output: True
